== Problem

+ Change `min` from 1 to 2 under `[ice.inputs.impact]` in
  `crates/mindtape/src/frameworks.toml`.
+ Run `just docs build`. The fact picks the change up:
  `www/generated/frameworks.json` now carries `"min": 2`.
+ 🔴 `www/public/mindtape/priority/index.html` comes out byte-identical and
  still renders `impact number 1–10`. Running `tola build --clean` in `www/`
  against the same fact renders `2–10`.
+ So `just docs check` validates HTML that no current source produced, which
  is the one thing every other derived-fact gate exists to stop.


== Environment

- Reproduced on `main` at `463e567`, Linux, tola 0.7.1, inside `nix develop`.
- Every fact-reading page is exposed, not just `/priority/`: `config.typ`,
  `cli.typ`, `dsl.typ`, `internals.typ`, `priority.typ`, and the five pages
  `1a4b7b0` converted to config slices.
- CI never sees it. A fresh checkout carries no `www/public/`, so its first
  build is already a clean one; this lies only on a developer's machine,
  where the gate is supposed to stop them.


== TO-BE

- 🟢 `just docs build` and `just docs check` re-render every page whose
  generated fact changed, so a stale page cannot reach `tola validate`.
- 🟢 The probe above, re-run, shows `2–10` on the built page.
- 🟢 The slower full rebuild is stated where the pipeline is described, not
  discovered by someone timing it.


== Changes

- `.just/docs.just` — `build` and `check` pass `--clean` to `tola build`,
  with the reason above each: tola does not track a `json()` dependency, so
  an incremental build serves HTML the current facts did not produce. Leave
  `serve` alone, which is a watch loop and not a gate.
- `docs/src/contributing/generated-docs.typ` — name the full rebuild and what
  buys it, so the cost reads as a decision rather than an oversight.
- `docs/contributing/generated-docs.md` — regenerated by `just docs md`,
  never hand-edited.


== Out of scope

- Teaching tola to track `json()` dependencies. That is upstream work, and
  the flag already gives a correct answer here.
- `just docs serve`, whose hot-reload loop is not a gate and would lose its
  whole point to a full rebuild per keystroke.


== Dogfood

This repo's docs are the only consumer. `just check` runs `docs-check` on
every commit, so the next change to any generated fact proves the gate
reacts instead of replaying a build from before it.

